## 2 : WHAT IS CACHING ?
=========================

Caching ek technique hai jisme frequently accessed data ki temporary copy ko faster storage layer me store kiya jata hai, 
taaki future read requests ke liye same data ko slower underlying system, jaise Database, se baar-baar retrieve na karna pade.
Cache khud koi specific technology nahi, balki ek concept/technique hai. 

Isko implement karne ke liye different technologies use ki ja sakti hain:

Redis → Distributed Cache
Caffeine → Local In-Memory Cache
Memcached → Distributed In-Memory Cache

## WITHOUT CACHE:
-------------------

Request
   ↓
Application
   ↓
Database
   ↓
Data


## WITH CACHE:
---------------

 Request
   ↓
Application
   ↓
 Cache
   ↓
Data Found?
   │
   ├── YES → Return Data
   │
   └── NO
        ↓
      Database
        ↓
      Data
        ↓
      Store in Cache
        ↓
      Return Data


Cache ka main purpose frequently accessed data ko cache se serve karke Database Load reduce karna hai.
Database Load kam hone se Database Response Time reduce ho sakta hai, jisse overall Application Performance improve hoti hai.


===============================
## 3 : CACHE HIT vs CACHE MISS
===============================

-------------
## CACHE HIT
-------------

Jab application requested data ko Cache me
successfully find kar leti hai, to ise Cache Hit kehte hain.

Is case me application directly Cache se data retrieve
karke response return kar deti hai, aur Database ko
hit karne ki zarurat nahi padti.

--------------
## CACHE MISS
--------------

Jab requested data Cache me available nahi hota,
to ise Cache Miss kehte hain.

Is case me application Database se data retrieve karti hai,
use future requests ke liye Cache me store karti hai,
aur phir response return karti hai.


==========================================
## 4 : WHY IS CACHE FASTER THAN DATABASE ?
==========================================

Caching ke commonly used implementations
frequently accessed data ko fast-access memory (RAM)
me store karte hain.

Cache se data retrieve karna generally fast hota hai,
kyunki commonly used caching implementations jaise Redis
data ko primarily RAM (memory) me store karti hain.

Iske comparison me Database ka primary persistent storage
generally SSD/HDD jaise disk storage par hota hai.

Database apni performance improve karne ke liye internally
frequently accessed data aur index pages ko apne Buffer Pool
(RAM) me cache karta hai.

Lekin Database query ko process karne me additional
overhead ho sakta hai, jaise:

    - Query processing
    - Index / data lookup
    - CPU computation
    - Possible disk I/O

Yaani:

    Database:
        Persistent Data → Disk (SSD / HDD)
        Internal Cache  → RAM (Buffer Pool)

    Cache:
        Primary Working Storage → RAM

        Normal cache reads/writes ke liye
        primarily RAM use hoti hai.

        Some cache implementations disk persistence
        support kar sakti hain, mainly data recovery /
        durability ke purpose se.


=======================
## 5 : REDIS OVERVIEW
=======================

Redis ek fast, in-memory data store hai jo
primarily data ko RAM (memory) me store karta hai.
Ye Application aur Database ke beech
ek fast-access data layer provide karta hai.

Redis ka primary working data RAM me hota hai,
lekin Redis durability / recovery ke liye
data ko disk par persist bhi kar sakta hai.

Caching ke context me Redis ko Application aur Database ke
beech ek external, distributed Cache ke roop me use kiya ja sakta hai,
jise multiple application instances access kar sakti hain.


-----------------------
##1 : KEY-VALUE MODEL
-----------------------

Redis fundamentally key-value data model provide karta hai.

Example:

    Key:
        product:101

    Value:
        {
            "id": 101,
            "name": "iPhone",
            "price": 79999
        }


Application:

    GET product:101
            ↓
          Redis
            ↓
    Corresponding Value



## QUESTION : REDIS KEY KAISE CREATE HOTI HAI ?
------------------------------------------------

Suppose request hai:

    GET /products/101

Controller ko path variable milta hai:

    productId = 101


Example:

    @GetMapping("/products/{productId}")

Application request se required identifier lekar
apni predefined naming convention ke according Redis Key banati hai.

Example:

    Redis Key = "product:" + productId

Result:

    product:101


## QUESTION : KYA KOI FIXED CONVENTION HAI?
--------------------------------------------

Nahi. Redis key ka koi fixed format force nahi karta.

Application / developer apni naming convention define karta hai.

Common pattern:

    <resource>:<identifier>

Example:

    product:101
    user:50
    order:999


-------------------------
##2: TTL (TIME TO LIVE)
-------------------------

Redis keys ke saath TTL (Time To Live) set kiya ja sakta hai.

Example:

    product:101
        ↓
    TTL = 10 minutes


TTL expire hone ke baad key available nahi rahegi.

Agar usi key ke liye next request aaye,
to data redis me available nahi hoga.

Application Database se fresh data retrieve karegi,
usse Redis me dobara cache karegi,
aur client ko response return karegi.


