## STALE-WHILE-REVALIDATE
---------------------------

Ye bhi ek approach hai jo popular cache entry ke expire hone ke
baad Cache Stampede ko prevent karne ke liye use ki ja sakti hai.

Basically normal caching scenario me har cache key ke saath ek TTL
(Time To Live) associated hota hai.

TTL expire hone ke baad corresponding key Redis se remove ho jaati hai.

Agar usi time us key ke corresponding data ke liye bahut saari concurrent requests aati hain,
to sabko Cache Miss mil sakta hai aur multiple requests backend /
Database ko hit kar sakti hain.


Stale-While-Revalidate approach me hum cache entry ki lifetime ko
logically do periods me divide karte hain:

    1. Fresh Time
    2. Stale Time


Example:

Database me:

    product:101
    price = ₹79,999


Hum is data ko Redis me cache karte hain.

Ab hum decide karte hain:

    Fresh Time = 10 minutes
    Stale Time = 5 minutes


Matlab:

First 10 minutes tak data ko fresh maana jayega.

Uske baad next 5 minutes tak data technically stale hoga,
lekin temporarily client ko serve karna allowed hoga.


So cache entry ko total:

10 min Fresh
      +
5 min Stale
--------------
15 minutes

tak Redis me available rakhna hoga.

Conceptually:

Redis TTL = Fresh Time + Stale Time

Yahan:

    Redis TTL = 15 minutes


