## AGAR REFRESH PROCESS BAHUT SLOW HO JAYE TO?
------------------------------------------------

Suppose background refresh start ho chuka hai, lekin Database
slow hone ki wajah se refresh complete hone me time lag raha hai.

Jab tak Redis key stale period ke andar available hai aur uska actual
TTL expire nahi hua hai, incoming requests stale data serve kar sakti hain.

Lekin agar refresh complete hone se pehle Redis TTL expire ho jata hai,
to cache entry remove ho jaayegi.

Uske baad normal Cache Miss handling karni padegi.

Agar usi time bahut saari concurrent requests aa jaati hain,
to Cache Stampede ka risk dobara aa sakta hai.

Isliye Stale Time ko sufficiently large rakhna important hai,
taaki ideally background refresh stale period ke andar hi
complete ho jaaye.

-----------------------------------------------------------
## LOCKING / REQUEST COALESCING VS STALE-WHILE-REVALIDATE
-----------------------------------------------------------

Jin requests ko particular cache entry ke liye Redis lock nahi mila:

Normal Locking:
→ Usually wait / retry karna padta hai until fresh data
  Cache me available ho jaaye.


Stale-While-Revalidate:
→ Wait karne ki zarurat nahi hoti.
  Already available stale data immediately return kar diya jata hai.

--------------------------------------------
## WHEN IS STALE-WHILE-REVALIDATE USEFUL?
--------------------------------------------

Stale-While-Revalidate especially useful hota hai jab:

1. Slightly stale data temporarily acceptable ho.

2. Cached data derived / aggregated ho aur har underlying
   data change par Cache Invalidation karna unnecessarily
   expensive ho.

3. Traffic high ho aur refresh ke time requests ko
   wait nahi karwana ho.



### EXAMPLE: TRENDING PRODUCTS LIST
-------------------------------------

Kabhi cache me jo data store hota hai, woh directly Database
ki kisi ek table ki single row se nahi aata.

Woh multiple tables aur other data sources se data combine karke
ya calculate karke banaya gaya hota hai.

Example:

        Product Views
        + Purchases
        + Likes
        + Recent Activity
                ↓
          Trending Score
                ↓
        Trending Products List


Ab underlying data continuously aur rapidly change ho raha hai.

Har view, purchase ya like ke baad Trending Products Cache ko
invalidate karna unnecessarily expensive ho sakta hai.

Saath hi, multiple tables / data sources se latest data fetch karke
Trending Products List ko on-the-go dobara calculate karne me
time lag sakta hai.

Ab agar aise high-traffic situation me bahut saari requests
latest data calculate hone ka wait karein, to response delay ho
sakta hai, jisse user experience kharab ho sakta hai.

Lekin agar Trending List kuch seconds ya minutes purani ho,
to bhi generally acceptable ho sakti hai.

Isliye aise cases me Fresh + Stale window use ki ja sakti hai.

Stale period ke dauran users ko temporarily existing data serve
kiya ja sakta hai, jisse requests ko latest data calculate hone ka
wait nahi karna padta.

Meanwhile, background me multiple tables / data sources se latest
data lekar Trending Products List dobara calculate karke Cache
refresh kar diya jata hai.



